      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5accc386-3e38-5eb8-a50c-5f5389f9f1c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Reynolds Channel, Nassau County, New York, Long Beach Barrier Island, Long Island, Barnum Island, Lawrence, Atlantic Beach, Rockaway Peninsula\n- Infrastructure: Atlantic Beach Bridge, NY 878, Seagirt Boulevard\n- People: William Reynolds\n\nFacts:\n- Reynolds Channel is a strait in Nassau County, New York, and it is named after William Reynolds.\n- Reynolds Channel separates the Long Beach Barrier Island from Long Island and Barnum Island.\n- The Long Beach Barrier Island contains the City of Long Beach and the villages of Atlantic Beach and Lido Beach.\n- The Atlantic Beach Bridge is a 153-foot-long toll drawbridge that carries NY 878.\n- The Atlantic Beach Bridge connects Lawrence and Atlantic Beach at Park Street, New York, and passes over the west end of Reynolds Channel.\n- The Atlantic Beach Bridge also provides direct access to the Rockaway Peninsula via Seagirt Boulevard.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
